      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A new technique is described for complex percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty of a lesion at the bifurcation of the obtuse marginal branch of the left coronary artery, just distal to a venous bypass graft insertion. Two separate angioplasty guide wire and catheter systems were used and the coronary artery side branch was protected in a \"crossing\" manner."},
